# PHASE 11 — DATABASE AND DATA MODEL

## 11. Choose a database

Use Supabase with PostgreSQL, Supabase Auth, and Storage as the preferred implementation unless the environment provides a compelling reason to use Firebase.

Before creating any external service, database project, bucket, or backend integration, ASK ME FOR PERMISSION.

Do not automatically create a Supabase or Firebase project.

Do not request secrets in public frontend configuration.

If I have not approved or configured a backend, continue building the frontend and integration interfaces. Provide an explicit setup checklist.

Use a repository abstraction so the application can operate against a clearly labeled local development dataset while the real backend is being configured.

The local dataset must never masquerade as production data.

## 11.1 Required database tables

